```json
{
  "paraphrased_article": {
    "headline_summary": "An Unconventional Royal Wedding in Norway",
    "body": "A clairvoyant princess from one of Europe's most enduring monarchies has tied the knot with a self-proclaimed sixth-generation shaman hailing from California. Despite the unconventional nature of the union, crowds gathered along the cloudy streets of Geiranger on Saturday afternoon, eager to catch sight of Princess Märtha Louise of Norway as she wed Durek Verrett.

At 52, Märtha Louise—the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja—holds the fourth position in the line of succession to Norway's throne. The traditional Church of Norway ceremony, which united her with 49-year-old Verrett, was held at the four-star Hotel Union, situated in a quaint village nestled below the Geiranger fjord, and welcomed both royalty and famous personalities.

Seven bridesmaids accompanied the princess down the aisle, among them her teenage daughters, Leah and Emma Behn, born of her previous marriage to Norwegian writer Ari Behn, who passed away after the couple divorced in 2017.

The celebration drew approximately 350 guests, with notable attendees including the bride's brother, Crown Prince Haakon, alongside his spouse Crown Princess Mette-Marit. Other royal guests featured Crown Princess Victoria of Sweden with Prince Daniel, as well as the Netherlands' Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien.

The princess's life has long deviated from typical royal norms. She has openly identified as a clairvoyant and, for ten years, operated a healing school where students were instructed in communicating with angels. In 2022, she revealed her decision to withdraw from official royal responsibilities, wanting to concentrate on the business ventures she shares with Verrett and to draw a sharper line between their personal enterprises and the Norwegian royal house.

On his Instagram profile, Verrett identifies himself as both a 'servant of God' and an 'energy activator.' His client list boasts prominent figures such as Gwyneth Paltrow, the founder of Goop, whom he has affectionately referred to as a 'soul sister.'"
  }
}
```

